 "explanation": {
  "concept": [
   "At C the exterior angle and the interior angle next to it lie on a straight line, so together they make 180°.",
   "The three interior angles also make 180°. Both pairs make 180° and share the angle at C, so the exterior angle equals the other two interior angles together."
  ],
  "visual": {
   "type": "triangle",
   "angles": [
    "39°",
    "112°",
    ""
   ],
   "exterior": "?"
  },
  "visualNote": "MISSING VISUAL CAPABILITY: the existing 'triangle' visual draws interior angles only; an extended side with an exterior angle cannot be drawn. Proposed: triangle + extended side + marked exterior angle (field 'exterior'). Until then, text only (structured givens; nothing is read from a picture)."
 },
